    "updated_at": "2022-08-24T16:53:23Z",
    "body": "> Please build starship with --locked to avoid unexpected changes in dependency versions.\r\n\r\nThanks, can you please add how to do this? \r\n\r\nI am hitting the same kinds of error messages trying to compile starship 1.10.2, cargo 1.63.0, macOS 12.5.1.\r\n\r\nAn older starship 1.9.1 builds fine. \r\n\r\nAm I understanding you correctly that the problem is in one of the dependencies (git-repository-0.21.1?) and that the dependency version could/should be marked as unusable/broken/invalid within the starship cargo toml?\r\n\r\nWhen I try the comment above in this thread, about about using --enforce-lock, then cargo shows these messages:\r\n\r\n```\r\nwarning: package `iana-time-zone v0.1.44` in Cargo.lock is yanked in registry `crates-io`, consider running without --locked\r\nwarning: package `pest v2.2.1` in Cargo.lock is yanked in registry `crates-io`, consider running without --locked\r\nwarning: package `pest_derive v2.2.1` in Cargo.lock is yanked in registry `crates-io`, consider running without --locked\r\nwarning: package `pest_generator v2.2.1` in Cargo.lock is yanked in registry `crates-io`, consider running without --locked\r\nwarning: package `pest_meta v2.2.1` in Cargo.lock is yanked in registry `crates-io`, consider running without --locked\r\n```\r\n\r\nBased on these messages, is it possible to change the comment above about using `--enforce-lock` because it is trying to use yanked info?\r\n\r\n",
