    "created_at": "2022-08-30T01:31:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-08-30T02:14:46Z",
    "body": "> `Cargo.toml` doesn't contain any transitive dependencies, which I think was the main culprit here. And the silent upgrades can be desirable in cases they do work (which it does most of the time).\r\n\r\nI noticed the issue described by IP as well, but it disappeared by itself after creating another release. The issue seems to be that somehow it manages to pull in `git-date:0.0.4` and `git-date:0.1.0` into the same dependency tree.\r\n\r\n**Update:** The issue still persists (when not using `--locked`), and I could reproduce it as well. Once the latest `master` of `starship` is released that should be fixed for good.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
