    "created_at": "2022-09-08T06:13:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-09-08T06:13:15Z",
    "body": "With all due respect.\r\n\r\nThe real question is how does this even happen. Let's first acknowledge that this is not the first time this kind of problem happens in starship. This happened before. My assessment of the issue is that someone accepts a PR and merges it, and it causes master (or whatever target the public uses) to break. Because rust's cargo lock file doesn't allow dependencies to change without your consent. Someone caused this.\r\n\r\nWell, what is CI doing in this case? Isn't this the job of CI prevent? You guys are using github actions as far as I can see. Something is wrong there, obviously.\r\n\r\nIt seems to me that everyone is talking about the symptom instead of talking about the real problem. Maybe I'm too ignorant to see how this is unavoidable and has to happen every couple of months, but hey, I can still dream that software never gets merged if it breaks master. I can still dream.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
