    "updated_at": "2022-09-08T07:10:30Z",
    "body": "@TheQuantumPhysicist I believe `master` pretty much never breaks, though running without `--locked` is not tested in CI. The issue is that not using `--locked` means that dependencies are used which were not yet available at the time of the release. It's impossible to test future upstream changes. The only way to fix this kind of issues is to contact upstream and have them yank incompatible versions, but nevertheless `--locked` is the official and only tested installation method.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
